                      "identifier": "18e7e79a-6719-419b-b385-86b4073db2c3",
                      "properties": {
                        "content": "<p>These terms apply to community.kentico.com (\"Kentico Community\"), operated by Kentico Software s.r.o. (\"Kentico\"). By creating an account you agree to these terms. Version {{TermsVersion}}, effective November, 2026.</p><ol><li><p><strong>Who can join.</strong> You must be at least 18 years old and provide a valid email address. One account per person.</p></li><li><p><strong>Your account.</strong> Keep your password safe; you're responsible for activity on your account. Tell us through <a href=\"~/support/feedback\">our feedback form</a> if you think it's been misused.</p></li><li><p><strong>How to behave.</strong> Be respectful and helpful. Don't post anything illegal, harassing, hateful, misleading, or infringing on others' rights. Don't post spam, advertising, malware, or other people's personal data. Don't post confidential information, including license keys, credentials or customer data. Don't try to break, overload or scrape the site.</p></li><li><p><strong>Your content.</strong> You keep ownership of what you post (questions, answers, comments, blog posts, contributions). You give Kentico a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, perpetual license to host, display, adapt, and distribute it on Kentico Community. Kentico may also feature it, with attribution, in Kentico Community emails, social media, and other Kentico channels. Only post content you have the right to share. Code you post may be used by others under the <a href=\"https://opensource.org/license/mit\">MIT License</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Moderation.</strong> Kentico may edit, hide or remove content, and may suspend or close accounts that break these terms. We'll usually tell you why.</p></li><li><p><strong>Leaving.</strong> You can close your account at any time through <a href=\"~/support/feedback\" data-pasted=\"true\">our feedback form</a>. We archive closed accounts, and your contributions stay, credited to you. If you ask us to erase your data, your contributions stay, credited to \"Former member\", as described in <a href=\"~/privacy\">Privacy</a>.</p></li><li><p><strong>No warranty.</strong> Kentico Community and its content (including answers from Kentico staff and other members) are provided \"as is\". Content isn't official Kentico product support, and it isn't a commitment about product features or roadmap. To the extent the law allows, Kentico isn't liable for loss from using the site or relying on its content.</p></li><li><p><strong>Changes.</strong> We may update these terms. If changes are significant, we’ll let you know by email or on the site.</p></li><li><p><strong>Contact.</strong> Send us a message through <a href=\"~/support/feedback\" data-pasted=\"true\">our feedback form</a>.</p></li></ol>"
